{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nvoid _show(const char *s, long long v) { cerr << s << '=' << v << '\\n'; }\ntemplate<typename... T>\nvoid _show(const char *s, long long v, T... rest) {\n  while(*s != ',') cerr << *s++;\n  cerr << '=' << v << ',';\n  _show(s + 1, rest...);\n}\ntemplate<typename T>\nostream& operator<<(ostream& os, const vector<T>& arr) {\n  os << '[';\n  for(const auto& elem : arr) os << elem << ',';\n  return os << ']';\n}\ntemplate<typename A, typename B>\nostream& operator<<(ostream& os, const pair<A,B>& p) {\n  return os << '(' << p.first << ',' << p.second << ')';\n}\n#define show(...) _show(#__VA_ARGS__, __VA_ARGS__)\n\nvector<long long> digits;\nlong long compute(long long num, long long depth) {\n  long long quotient = num / digits[depth];\n  num %= digits[depth];\n  if(num == 0) return quotient * depth;\n  return quotient * depth + min(depth + compute(digits[depth] - num, depth - 1), compute(num, depth - 1));\n}\nint main() {\n  ios::sync_with_stdio(false); cin.tie(nullptr);\n  \n  long long cases = 1, value;\n  long long current = 0;\n  while(digits.size() < 17) {\n    digits.push_back(current);\n    current = current * 10 + 1;\n  }\n  while(cases--) {\n    cin >> value;\n    cout << compute(value, 16);\n  }\n  return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    private static List<Long> digits = new ArrayList<>();\n    \n    private static void show(String s, long v) {\n        System.err.println(s + \"=\" + v);\n    }\n    \n    private static long compute(long num, long depth) {\n        long quotient = num / digits.get((int)depth);\n        num %= digits.get((int)depth);\n        if (num == 0) {\n            return quotient * depth;\n        }\n        long option1 = depth + compute(digits.get((int)depth) - num, depth - 1);\n        long option2 = compute(num, depth - 1);\n        return quotient * depth + Math.min(option1, option2);\n    }\n    \n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        \n        long current = 0;\n        while (digits.size() < 17) {\n            digits.add(current);\n            current = current * 10 + 1;\n        }\n        \n        long cases = 1;\n        while (cases-- > 0) {\n            long value = scanner.nextLong();\n            System.out.println(compute(value, 16));\n        }\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.85\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0001255195093108341, -2.264974000354414e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -8.642300235806033e-05, -2.5629668016335927e-05, -0.04864013195037842, -0.2820259928703308, -0.00043478095903992653, -8.344646857949556e-07, -2.455681169521995e-05, -0.01603505201637745, -0.00023314618738368154, -0.062333378940820694, -1.3708974620385561e-05, -0.21494188904762268, -2.455681169521995e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.003278121817857027, -7.1